<Legal title="Cancellation and Refunds" description="How to cancel a Spending Atlas subscription, and the free trial and refund terms.">
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <strong>In short:</strong> Cancel any time and keep using your plan until the end of the period. Cancel during the trial and you pay nothing. Anyone who asks within 14
      days of a payment gets a refund.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Cancelling your subscription</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in on the website and open the <a href="/en/account/subscription">My subscription</a> page.</li>
    <li>Tap “Cancel” and confirm the cancellation on the Paddle page that opens.</li>
    <li>Plan features stay available until the last day of the period and you are not charged for the next one. Your records are kept; you continue on the Free plan.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Subscriptions bought through a mobile app store (App Store, Google Play) must be cancelled in that store’s subscription settings.</p>

  <h2>Free trial</h2>
  <p>If you cancel before the 7-day trial ends, nothing is charged. If you have not cancelled by the end of the trial, the first period’s fee is charged.</p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Within 14 days:</strong> you can request a refund within 14 days of your first payment or a renewal. The full amount is refunded to the card you paid with.
    </li>
    <li><strong>After 14 days:</strong> past periods are not refunded; if you cancel, you keep access until the end of the period.</li>
    <li><strong>Plan upgrades:</strong> a difference payment is subject to the same 14-day rule.</li>
    <li>If you could not use plan features because of a fault in the Service, write to us regardless of timing; we will review it and give a partial or full refund.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Use the link in the invoice email from Paddle, or write to <Fill k="eposta" label="E-posta" /> from your account’s email address. Once approved, the amount reaches your card
    within 14 days at the latest; depending on your bank it may take a few more days to appear on your statement. A refunded subscription ends immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>Your statutory rights</h2>
  <p>
    These terms do not limit the right of withdrawal in the <a href="/en/legal/distance-sales">Distance Sales Agreement</a> or your rights under Turkish Consumer Protection Law
    No. 6502.
  </p>
</Legal>
